And then, I'm going to select
the columns, miles per gallon,

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:53.730
cylinder, displacement,
and horsepower.

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:55.915
So if we look at the--

00:16:55.915 --> 00:16:59.582
scroll this down-- if we look
at that data frame cars data set

00:16:59.582 --> 00:17:01.040
before we do anything
else, you can

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.950
see that has a lot of
columns, so miles per gallon,

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:06.230
all the way up to carb.

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:08.359
And we can see that
cylinder is labeled here

00:17:08.359 --> 00:17:09.829
as a double, which
actually means

00:17:09.829 --> 00:17:12.319
that it's as a numeric value.

00:17:12.319 --> 00:17:14.930
When we do this
transformation here,

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:20.010
we take that data set, and then
change cylinder to be a factor,

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:23.060
and then select only
